Films such as 3M Wrap Film Series 2080 and Avery Dennison Supreme Wrapping Film are solid colour through the material, and 3M describes 2080 as usable out of the box with or without graphic protection. A clear wrap overlaminate is an option for a different sheen or extra protection, not a requirement. Our guide to <a href=\"/gloss-vs-satin-vs-matte-car-wrap-finish/\">gloss, satin and matte finishes</a> covers those choices.</li>\n<li><strong>Cut vinyl lettering and decals.</strong> Lettering cut from coloured cast film has no ink to protect. It is installed bare, which is one reason <a href=\"/truck-lettering-and-decals-toronto/\">truck lettering and decals</a> are such a durable, low-cost option.</li>\n<li><strong>Short-term printed promotions.</strong> A graphic that will be removed in a few months, on a flat panel, in mild conditions, may be run unlaminated to save cost. It will not carry a manufacturer''s long-term warranty, and that is a reasonable trade for a short campaign.</li>\n<li><strong>Perforated window film.</strong> This is a special case with its own clear overlaminate designed to keep the perforations open; see our article on <a href=\"/perforated-window-film-one-way-vision/\">perforated window film</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Gloss, Luster or Matte: The Laminate Sets the Finish</h2>\n<p>Because the vehicle wrap laminate is the top surface, it decides how the wrap looks. Printed vinyl is normally gloss white; the laminate then makes the finished wrap gloss, luster (a soft semi-gloss) or matte.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Gloss</strong> is the default for commercial wraps. Colours look deepest, and it is the easiest to clean.</li>\n<li><strong>Luster</strong> cuts reflections, which helps photographs of the vehicle and reduces glare on large flat panels such as box sides.</li>\n<li><strong>Matte</strong> gives a printed wrap the flat look of a matte paint job. It shows fingerprints and oils more, and some stains that would wipe off gloss are harder to remove from a matte surface.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Choose the finish for the whole fleet at once. A gloss van parked beside a matte one with the same artwork reads as two different brands.</p>\n\n<h2>Cast Laminate Over Cast Film: Matching the System</h2>\n<p>A vehicle wrap laminate is made the same two ways print films are, cast or calendered, and the same rules apply. 3M''s current overlaminate line-up for fleet vehicles lists a 3 mil non-cast gloss laminate rated for flat surfaces with an expected life of up to 4 years, alongside 2 mil cast laminates rated for flat to curved surfaces at up to 8 years, and a 1.2 mil cast laminate described as its most conformable. The thinner cast laminates are the ones that go over a wrap with recesses, rivets or compound curves.</p>\n<p>Manufacturers publish matched systems for a reason. 3M''s IJ180 print film lists specific recommended overlaminates, and a wrap built from a listed film, laminate and ink combination is what qualifies for its finished-graphic warranty programmes. Mixing a cast print film with a cheaper calendered laminate saves money on the roll and gives you a sheet that behaves like calendered film in every curve. Our article on <a href=\"/cast-vs-calendered-vinyl-wrap-film/\">cast vs calendered vinyl</a> explains why that matters.</p>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Subaru-Sambar-Full-Wrap-Driverss-Side-Front-1024x538.png\" alt=\"Laminated printed full wrap conforming to the curves of a Subaru Sambar\" width=\"1024\" height=\"538\" loading=\"lazy\" /><figcaption>A laminated print film still has to follow every curve, which is why the laminate must be as conformable as the film beneath it.</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>The Step Nobody Sees: Letting the Print Dry First</h2>\n<p>Solvent and eco-solvent inks keep releasing solvent for hours after printing. If a print is laminated too soon, that solvent is trapped between the two films and the 3M bulletins list the consequences: insufficient drying can cause overlaminate lifting, a film that becomes soft and stretchy, and poor graphic performance. 3M also notes that graphic failure from insufficient drying time is not covered by its warranty. A good shop builds drying time into the schedule. If a printed wrap is promised the morning after it was printed, ask how the print was dried.</p>\n\n<h2>What to Ask When You Get a Printed Wrap Quote</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Is the wrap laminated, and with what?</strong> The answer should be a product name that matches the print film''s manufacturer and construction.</li>\n<li><strong>What finish?</strong> Gloss, luster or matte, decided for the whole fleet.</li>\n<li><strong>Is the film, laminate and ink combination warranted as a system?</strong> If the shop is 3M or Avery Dennison certified, ask whether the job qualifies for the manufacturer''s finished-graphic warranty and what it covers.</li>\n<li><strong>How long does the print cure before lamination?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>These sit alongside the broader questions in our <a href=\"/vehicle-wrap-checklist-before-you-buy/\">vehicle wrap checklist</a>, and our guide to <a href=\"/full-colour-print-wrap-vs-colour-change/\">full colour print vs colour change wraps</a> explains where the printed route makes sense in the first place.</p>\n\n<h2>Caring for a Laminated Wrap</h2>\n<p>A vehicle wrap laminate makes a printed wrap easier to live with, not maintenance-free. Hand washing with a pH-neutral soap, keeping pressure washers away from edges, and removing fuel, bird droppings and tar promptly are the habits that get a laminated wrap to the far end of its expected life. Our <a href=\"/top-8-maintenance-tips-for-vehicle-wraps/\">maintenance tips for vehicle wraps</a> and our <a href=\"/fleet-wrap-replacement-schedule-guide/\">fleet wrap replacement schedule</a> cover the long-term routine.</p>\n\n<h2>Get the Right Laminate on Your Printed Wrap</h2>\n<p>For a printed <a href=\"/commercial-vehicle-wraps/\">commercial vehicle wrap</a> that has to look sharp for years, the laminate is not the place to save. Vinyl Wrap Toronto prints on 3M and Avery Dennison cast films and laminates them with the manufacturer''s matched overlaminate in the finish you choose. To talk through a printed wrap for your van, truck or fleet, <a href=\"/contact/\">request a quote</a> or call <a href=\"tel:416-746-1381\">416-746-1381</a>.</p>\n\n<p><em>Sources: 3M Product Bulletin, Scotchcal Graphic Film IJ40C; 3M Product Bulletin, <a href=\"https://multimedia.3m.com/mws/media/1879697O/3m-product-bulletin-ij180c-en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Controltac Graphic Film IJ180C</a>; 3M, <a href=\"https://multimedia.3m.com/mws/media/2578894O/3m-overlaminates-for-fleet-vehicles-sell-sheet-print-only.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Overlaminates for Fleet Vehicles</a>; 3M Product Bulletin, Wrap Film Series 2080; Avery Dennison <a href=\"https://graphics.averydennison.com/content/dam/averydennison/graphics/eu/en/Data-Sheets/DIM/ds-Avery-Dennison-MPI-1105-wrapping-series-EN.pdf.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">MPI 1105 Wrapping Series data sheet</a>.</em></p>\n","style":"text-align:start;font-family:\"Poppins\", Sans-serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.5em;font-weight:300"}]},{"width":25,"background":"#F8F8F8","padding":"10px 10px 10px 10px","blocks":[{"type":"toc","title":"Table of Contents","box":"background-color:#F8F8F8"},{"type":"form"}]}]}]}]', datetime('now')
